-- title

vidDeck

A wrapper around a youtube web page
that provides global hotkey to control
the video while your in other apps on macOS.

This is primarily a personal project to make
it easier to take notes on videos by using
hotkeys to control the video while still in
a notes app. You're welcome to use it if
it works for you. 


-- h2

Installation

- Download the vidDeck_0.1.0_aarch64.dmg
file from the releases/macos directory
in this repo, open it, and move the vidDeck
app to your Applications folder. Then,
launch it from there. 


-- notes

- This is very much a "works-on-my-machine"
project. If it doesn't work on yours
you'll need to figure out why yourself. 

- The start/stop button rewinds a few seconds
when you restart a video. Makes it
easier to pick up the thread for notes. 

- You can map Stream Deck buttons to
the hotkeys to control videos that way. 

- I'm not sure if you'll need to
do the thing where you right click
to open the app or not (based on the
macOS security settings)

- For some reason my app launcher
doesn't see the app. I have to
double click it directly from
the Applications folder. 

- I'm not sure what browser is used
behind the scenes, but YouTube gives
me an error on live chat windows
saying it's too old for
live chat to work. 


-- h2

The Hotkeys

{{Option + Shift + S}} - start/stop

{{Option + Shift + A}} - rewind 

{{Option + Shift + E}} - fast forward

{{Option + Shift + Z}} - slow down

{{Option + Shift + C}} - speed up


-- h2

